                        "target_lang_word": "Turmkugel",
                        "target_lang_code": "de",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": []
                    },
                    {
                        "translation_id": "3a0ec44f-d114-4f04-b1bb-b449a2487677",
                        "source_entry_id": "ffa77421-d3c5-3ea4-ae5d-25e693b81135",
                        "source_sense_id": "a5f468f5-735f-3b7f-9f98-c0bdafeeae08",
                        "source_sense_description": "een ornament op een markant punt van een bouwwerk",
                        "target_lang_word": "Dachknauf",
                        "target_lang_code": "de",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": []
                    },
                    {
                        "translation_id": "0c9b7f17-d306-48d2-8070-47921f83d450",
                        "source_entry_id": "ffa77421-d3c5-3ea4-ae5d-25e693b81135",
                        "source_sense_id": "a5f468f5-735f-3b7f-9f98-c0bdafeeae08",
                        "source_sense_description": "een ornament op een markant punt van een bouwwerk",
                        "target_lang_word": "finial",
                        "target_lang_code": "en",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "finial",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "a73843fa-6c5b-3361-beb6-b9918cc7a380",
                                        "entry_id": "ea13ff0c-d32b-3c7f-bee8-b780b952719d",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Especially in Gothic architecture: an ornament, often in the form of a bunch or knot of foliage, on the peak of the gable of a roof, a pediment, a pinnacle, etc."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "a4e12dcf-e839-4ebe-89d6-1bce104d1887",
                                                "sense_id": "a73843fa-6c5b-3361-beb6-b9918cc7a380",
                                                "text": "[O]f that money vvhich aroſe of their amercements, vvere certain gilded ſhields made, vvhich vvere ſet up on the finial or lantern of Jupiters Temple."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "7b18e470-9734-40a7-9201-b437b6a1709f",
                                                "sense_id": "a73843fa-6c5b-3361-beb6-b9918cc7a380",
                                                "text": "His [Butades'] invention it vvas to ſet up Gargils or Antiques at the top of a Gavill end, as a finiall to the creſt tiles, vvhich in the beginning he called Protypa."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "a3f2f63d-2133-4b02-b816-44efbfb74a7f",
                                                "sense_id": "a73843fa-6c5b-3361-beb6-b9918cc7a380",
                                                "text": "From this fair Palace then he takes his Front, / From that his Finials; […] / And ſo, ſelecting euery vvhere the beſt, / Doth thirty Models in one Houſe digeſt."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "8f00f2b1-2596-4eeb-a0b1-32b15c2da462",
                                                "sense_id": "a73843fa-6c5b-3361-beb6-b9918cc7a380",
                                                "text": "Truth uncompromisingly told will always have its ragged edges; hence the conclusion of such a narration is apt to be less finished than an architectural finial."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "8d2caea1-b519-4ec9-a6d8-24a4e7e16235",
                                                "sense_id": "a73843fa-6c5b-3361-beb6-b9918cc7a380",
                                                "text": "The steep slate roofs were topped with bronze finials so tall and fanciful they looked like drops of liquid sliding down a thread."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "f72de463-b391-32e3-909f-d1fff2d3dff9",
                                        "entry_id": "ea13ff0c-d32b-3c7f-bee8-b780b952719d",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Any decorative fitting on the corner, end, or top of an object such as a canopy, a fencepost, a flagpole, a curtain rod, or the newel post of a staircase."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "broadly"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "9c443a12-27b0-4c0a-88da-ee8077b9f0c8",
                                                "sense_id": "f72de463-b391-32e3-909f-d1fff2d3dff9",
                                                "text": "The finial is also of timber (probably oak) and is of the rather elaborate type, originally favoured by the London & South Western Railway for its timber masts."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "e7c17200-af7d-4b34-b602-acf65cb79c16",
                                                "sense_id": "f72de463-b391-32e3-909f-d1fff2d3dff9",
                                                "text": "It was a narrow, gravelled island we had to lie on, guarded by glazed brick chimneys and, running along the sides, a prickly little gothic fence of iron finials and terracotta quatrefoils."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "ffb65781-7527-4dfd-9d84-a2aab3c64fa4",
                                                "sense_id": "f72de463-b391-32e3-909f-d1fff2d3dff9",
                                                "text": "Mark Twain called the cherimoya \"deliciousness itself,\" though others have described this heart-shaped, fist-sized fruit with pale-green leathery skin as \"reptilian,\" like a \"fossil artichoke\" or \"the finial for a giant four-poster bed.\""
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "728c94b5-15ef-455e-9b77-0bce02663610",
                                                "sense_id": "f72de463-b391-32e3-909f-d1fff2d3dff9",
                                                "text": "He says there's a very particular etiquette to having your flag at half-mast: you're supposed to first run it all the way up to the finial at the top and then bring it halfway down."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "698f57cd-3fd8-44df-91fd-999fb475132c",
                                                "sense_id": "f72de463-b391-32e3-909f-d1fff2d3dff9",
                                                "text": "For several years, the finial was missing, and its replica replacement will save the wooden post from rotting."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "215d5aa6-c0b7-39bc-9af1-7005b5edad9f",
                                        "entry_id": "ea13ff0c-d32b-3c7f-bee8-b780b952719d",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "The completion or end of something."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "also",
                                            "attributive",
                                            "figuratively"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "fcbc5457-7a5e-4ba7-ab5d-a3bfa264e0c9",
                                                "sense_id": "215d5aa6-c0b7-39bc-9af1-7005b5edad9f",
                                                "text": "But, as the Phœnix on my Front doth gliſter, / Thou ſhalt the Finials of my Frame illuſtre."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "e042a9e9-9a34-400a-b020-62bbfc44f185",
                                                "sense_id": "215d5aa6-c0b7-39bc-9af1-7005b5edad9f",
                                                "text": "[T]hey have invented idols, a manifest advance toward that polytheism and pantheism which lead through a triad and duad of deities to monotheism, the finial of the spiritual edifice."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "351daac3-a4bf-42a4-883b-669606a8fa2e",
                                                "sense_id": "215d5aa6-c0b7-39bc-9af1-7005b5edad9f",
                                                "text": "[…] Lancelot Carnaby stopped from his rash venture into the water, and drew himself back into an ivied bush, which served as the finial of the little garden-hedge."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "translation_id": "06234435-822a-42c5-ab7d-c36ba7a11b58",
                        "source_entry_id": "ffa77421-d3c5-3ea4-ae5d-25e693b81135",
